    "body": "## Summary\n- introduce a dedicated `JOB_PUBLICATION_FUNDING` wallet transaction type for Stripe money credited specifically for job publication\n- keep ordinary and legacy Stripe wallet top-ups classified as `TOP_UP`\n- derive the wallet ledger transaction type from the already-validated settlement purpose\n- add regression coverage that pins both publication funding and ordinary top-ups to the correct wallet transaction type\n\n## Why\nThe payment ledger already persists `JOB_PUBLICATION` versus `TOP_UP`, but wallet credits were still always written as `TOP_UP`. That made finance/audit views lose the commercial source of funds even though Stripe settlement identity was known. This slice keeps the payment ledger and wallet ledger semantically aligned without changing balances or idempotency keys.\n\n## Migration\nNo Flyway migration is required. Wallet transaction type is stored as a string and the new enum value is additive.\n\n## Validation\nDo not merge until all latest-head required CI/checks complete successfully.",
