          "pull_request": {
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jedreekPrograms/dofast/pulls/104",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/jedreekPrograms/dofast/pull/104",
            "diff_url": "https://github.com/jedreekPrograms/dofast/pull/104.diff",
            "patch_url": "https://github.com/jedreekPrograms/dofast/pull/104.patch",
            "merged_at": "2026-08-29T07:58:08Z"
          },
          "body": "## Summary\n- reconcile Stripe wallet ledger type with persisted settlement purpose\n- require `JOB_PUBLICATION` claims to map to `JOB_PUBLICATION_FUNDING` and ordinary `TOP_UP` claims to map to `TOP_UP`\n- treat orphaned Stripe wallet credits of either type as reconciliation mismatches\n- add a database-backed smoke scenario covering healthy publication funding, wrong wallet type, and orphan detection\n- update publish-with-payment ledger documentation to match the production semantics introduced in #103\n\n## Why\n#103 made the wallet ledger preserve the commercial source of Stripe publication funding, but finance reconciliation still assumed every Stripe credit was a `TOP_UP`. That would flag valid publication funding incorrectly and did not detect orphaned `JOB_PUBLICATION_FUNDING` entries. This slice makes the audit invariant match the actual settlement model.\n\n## Migration\nNo Flyway migration is required; this is reconciliation logic, smoke coverage and documentation only.\n\n## Validation\nDo not merge until all latest-head required CI/checks complete successfully.",
